<pending_commit branch="chromeos-5.41" change_id="I934580c05fdf63311d7ccabee5bf5c8232c441b8" commit="69e154eba8ae940b4b258ea190a2e56a891f970c" commit_message="FROMLIST: monitor/rfcomm: Fix a potential memory access issue for compatibility with LLVM  This patch removes &quot;packed&quot; attribute from the definition of struct rfcomm_rpn to prevent the access to an unaligned struct member in mmc_rpn(). This patch also introduces a temp variable in mcc_pn() to prevent unaligned access without touching the definition of struct rfcomm_pn, since struct rfcomm_pn is used as a PDU.  (cherry picked from http://www.spinics.net/lists/linux-bluetooth/msg69149.html)  BUG=chromium:665653 TEST=emerge bluez with LLVM enforced  Change-Id: I934580c05fdf63311d7ccabee5bf5c8232c441b8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414227 Commit-Ready: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414227" owner_email="mcchou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/bluez" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/bluez" ref="refs/changes/27/414227/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idbdc963ba077a14efad9eea3b047f35a5a605bd6" commit="b847e75af2f2d43f30c163a27a7e711800067366" commit_message="servo_v4: Added initial USB PD support for both CHG/DUT ports  - CHG port can connect as SNK at different voltage levels - DUT port presents as SNK only - DUT port uses fixed polarity since it has a fixed cable - Not supporting ALT or ALT_DP modes in terms of svdm messages at   this point. - No support yet for USB mux.  BUG=chromium:571476 BRANCH=None TEST=Manual CHG port: Tested with Zinger and Plankton and 5/12/20V VBUS levels. DUT port: Tested against Reef and verified that port reached SNK_READY.  Change-Id: Idbdc963ba077a14efad9eea3b047f35a5a605bd6 Signed-off-by: Scott &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419117 Commit-Ready: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="419117" owner_email="scollyer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/17/419117/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I875a97f6776f7c939f66ed1051b2ddab8211ae72" commit="5e1bad86b72b692be0e1ce15d0fcb639a9010103" commit_message="device: Add MosysFanControl for Chromeboxes.  Chromeboxes (for instance, beltino reference boards) control fan by running mosys. Add a reference implementation (copied from beltino factory branch) into fan module.  BUG=None TEST=make test  Change-Id: I875a97f6776f7c939f66ed1051b2ddab8211ae72 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/420185 Commit-Ready: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="420185" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/85/420185/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie7e62cb0b2eda49b04a592ee1d0903e83246b045" commit="752b773945a016ad2d41223290b7f2efdebad804" commit_message="cr50: keep wp and console state through deep sleep  After every reboot, we were resetting the write protect and console lock states back to default. With this change the wp and lock states will be preserved through deep sleep. They will still be reset on any other type of reboot (like Power On reset or panic).  The states are also cleared if the system detects a rollback even when booting from the deep sleep.  With this patch it is going to be impossible to remove hardware write protection guarding writes into AP and EC firmware flash, unless the cr50 console is unlocked.  Locking the console would reinstate hardware write protection automatically even if it was disabled when the console was unlocked.  Two long life scratch register 1 bits are used to keep the console and write protect states over resets. To make code cleaner bitmap assignments of the long life scratch register is put in its own include file.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58961 BRANCH=none TEST=manual  On prod/dev images verify that the default wp and console lock  states are still correct.   change the lock and write protect states from the default and  verify they are preserved through deep sleep.   reboot cr50 and make sure that they are reset.   unlock the console and enable flash writes, then set fallback  counter on cr50 to the value of 6 (rw 0x40000128 1; rw  0x4000012c 6) and put the AP into deep sleep by hitting  Alt-H-VolUp.   In five minutes press the power button on the device to bring  it back from s5. Observe cr50 fall back to an older image and  console lock and wp disabled.  Change-Id: Ie7e62cb0b2eda49b04a592ee1d0903e83246b045 Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/420812 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="420812" owner_email="mruthven@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/12/420812/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="arc-12.1.0-pre2" change_id="Ic23fdc8c6d8c028603ff9fd3b18a6903dd29302e" commit="94a5f1a1ead4d57e45481edf13fa7a0811d37852" commit_message="FROMLIST: configure.ac: Respect LLVM_CFLAGS in LLVM version detection  When compiling LLVM headers, including llvm-config.h, we need to respect LLVM_CFLAGS. This is especially crucial if LLVM is located in a non-standard location and it happens that llvm-config.h includes another header. In such case the detection would fail due to missing header, because the path is provided in LLVM_CFLAGS.  Let's add LLVM_CFLAGS to global CFLAGS for the time of detection and then restore the original flags, as done in other places of the script.  Signed-off-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/127290/) Signed-off-by: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/127290/)  BUG=b:33533853 BUG=b:33281615 TEST=emerge-amd64-generic-cheets arc-mesa against nyc-mr1-arc  Change-Id: Ic23fdc8c6d8c028603ff9fd3b18a6903dd29302e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/421253 Commit-Ready: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nicolas Norvez &lt;norvez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="421253" owner_email="norvez@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/mesa" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/mesa" ref="refs/changes/53/421253/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3b3a6fc10d7715cf83103f67e272ccc3a216efb0" commit="4e3dfedc4727511cb7540a69d5fd9b907941ad77" commit_message="[autotest] Fix dut_status_unittest time comparisons.  The logic for unit testing `dut-status --until` was wrong.  It was supposed to test the &quot;--until&quot; value was &quot;now&quot; in the sense that it was in-between two timestamps that bracketed the calculation of the value.  One of the comparisons was for &quot;&lt;=&quot; instead of &quot;&gt;=&quot;, leading to occasional flake.  This changes to use a mock to force `time.time()` to return a pre-computed value.  This change also contains other miscellaneous (non-functional) clean-up of the unit tests.  BUG=chromium:675667 TEST=run the unit tests using a patch to provoke the bug.  Change-Id: I3b3a6fc10d7715cf83103f67e272ccc3a216efb0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422427 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="422427" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/27/422427/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1f07b0fedfcd36971ddebb794a1f60292d8d766d" commit="433abb0c38f71de5d42cbcc73ad4801a92b15be1" commit_message="init: execute &quot;goofy_control start&quot; at background.  The process of goofy_control does not stop, so it wound block other init script in main.d/ to execute. Now we execute it at background to avoid blocking other scripts.  BUG=b:33766281 TEST=test at the device  Change-Id: I1f07b0fedfcd36971ddebb794a1f60292d8d766d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422588 Commit-Ready: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="422588" owner_email="akahuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/88/422588/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I861ba108e603ef430b3efa3582cd4797653fe7fb" commit="1bd520fca0e649baa5dcf5f97a42bfced11344a9" commit_message="usb_probe: support bus_id and multiple vid:pid's  1. Use dut api 2. Add an optional bus_id filter 3. Replace vid and pid by a list of strings in format 'VID:PID' to support searching for multiple devices.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:60896 TEST=Run usb_probe test  Change-Id: I861ba108e603ef430b3efa3582cd4797653fe7fb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422708 Commit-Ready: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="422708" owner_email="phoenixshen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/08/422708/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I9d1ea30ad3cdf7b2c6a16823dcc733995bb1f686" commit="f82b0c702db1218b85a153402c79abf746553b0a" commit_message="Compile I2C_CHARDEV into the 4.4 kernel  In order to make the /dev/i2c-* devices appear during boot we need to compile this driver into the kernel instead of having it as a module. We need those devices at boot so we can perform firmware updates during the boot process to touch devices connected via I2C.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:61088 TEST=built the kernel and deployed on an Eve.  During boot the devices are present.  Change-Id: I9d1ea30ad3cdf7b2c6a16823dcc733995bb1f686 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422907 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="422907" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/07/422907/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9107.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>